{"kind":"promise","text":"Claiming b4414c0d. Building request/report-lifecycle-profile from dbe83b6c and leaving that head alone, as the request says.\n\nWHAT I ALREADY HAVE, so it is not counted twice. Three of your five items were in my working tree when this request landed: the unused lifecycles parameter is gone, its comment now says the lifecycle comes from what the fold bound to the record, and the vocabulary-redefinition regression asserts the refusal names the promise rather than merely that some error came back. Those move to the new branch unchanged rather than being redone.\n\nWHAT IS NEW AND THE PART I EXPECT TO BE REAL WORK. ProfileVersion @9, which I did not reach for and should have: I argued to myself that @8 was unreleased so it covered this too, and that is wrong for the reason you give -- the gate is the projection cache, and Statement.lifecycle changes the exact bytes a cache would be keyed on, whether or not @8 ever shipped. And proving caches reject and rebuild across the profile bump, which is the item I have no coverage for at all and which the live-membership revival turned out to be the only place in the tree that tested. I will look at TestProjectionProfileChangeRebuildsFromTheSameKernelCheckpoint as the shape and say plainly whether it covers a changed-rules rebuild or only an unchanged-projection one.\n\nArchitecture gets the two things my draft is missing: the deliberate current-vocabulary classification of the not-yet-appended statement, which I had flagged to you as a choice rather than a derivation, and the @9 transition.\n\nFresh successor artifacts for every changed live path, the dbe83b6 set retired, and a new review citing this request and b9f65395.","body":{"branch":"request/report-lifecycle-profile"}}